proc:CM-1-4 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1 ;
    skos:definition "Information Technology Includes Processes Related To Providing IT Support Across Commercial Operations. It Covers Strategy, Delivery & Governance Processes. Commercial Information Technology Includes Hardware, Software & Communication Infrastructure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "IT Services"@en .

proc:L1-ehs-gov-reporting a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "Protect people, assets, and the environment through process safety; occupational health and safety; environmental management and compliance; emergency preparedness and response; incident, release, and near-miss management; corrective-action learning; and required regulatory reporting to government authorities."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "EHS & Gov Reporting"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "This domain governs EHS management, environmental and safety compliance, required regulator-facing reporting, and the enterprise coordination of incidents, releases, investigations, corrective actions, and emergency response. It does not replace operational ownership: operating sites, asset owners, maintenance, logistics, product stewardship, and business functions remain accountable for safely executing their work, preventing and containing events, and completing assigned corrective actions. Legal & Corporate Communications advises on legal privilege, enforcement exposure, disclosure, litigation hold, regulator strategy, and approved internal/external communications when those dimensions arise."@en .

proc:L1-finance a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "Planning, recording, controlling, reporting, and managing the financial resources, performance, obligations, and risks of the downstream business, including financial planning and analysis, accounting, reporting, payroll, treasury, tax, and internal financial controls."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Finance"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Includes budgeting, forecasting, financial and management accounting, period close, statutory and management reporting, accounts payable, expense reimbursement, payroll, treasury, liquidity and cash management, tax, financial compliance, internal controls, audit support, and financial risk management. Supports commercial, supply-chain, refining, midstream, distribution, and enabling-function processes through financial governance, measurement, and transaction processing. Excludes operational execution in those business domains and fixed-asset project accounting where it is intentionally governed and executed as an ERP-native capability outside this taxonomy's modeled scope."@en .

proc:L1-human-resources a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "The function that plans, attracts, develops, rewards, engages, retains, and transitions the workforce to enable the downstream business, including workforce planning, talent acquisition, onboarding, learning and development, performance management, compensation and benefits, employee and labor relations, HR policy and compliance, workforce information, and HR service delivery."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Human Resources"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Includes workforce strategy and planning; organizational and position management; recruiting, sourcing, selection, hiring, and onboarding; learning, development, performance, talent, succession, and career management; compensation, benefits, recognition, and payroll-input administration; employee and labor relations; workforce policy, employment compliance, ethics-related workforce processes, and employee communications; workforce data, HR information systems, people analytics, and HR service delivery; and employee transition, redeployment, separation, and retirement. Human Resources owns workforce policies, people processes, employee experience, and workforce information. It provides authorized employee, time, attendance, compensation, and deduction inputs to payroll; Finance or a designated payroll service owns pay calculation, payment execution, withholding/remittance, payroll accounting, and financial control."@en .

proc:L1-legal-corp-comm a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "Provide legal counsel and legal-risk management, including contract and transaction support, litigation and dispute resolution, regulatory and compliance advice, corporate governance and entity support, and management of external legal providers; develop and deliver internal corporate communications and approved enterprise messaging."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Legal & Corp Comm"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "In scope: general counsel and legal advice to management and functions; legal review and support for contracts, transactions, claims, disputes, investigations, and litigation; regulatory interpretation and legal/compliance advice; corporate governance, entity management, board/committee administration where retained in the function, and corporate records; intellectual-property and outside-counsel management where not separate domains; employee, leadership, change, policy, crisis, and enterprise-wide internal communications; approval, stewardship, and consistency of official corporate messages. Out of scope (Step 8 decision): government relations, lobbying, and industry-association engagement; investor relations, shareholder engagement, and external board relations; public relations, media relations, community relations, philanthropy, and external reputation campaigns; distributor incentives, trade discounts, channel allowances, and other commercial-program design."@en .

proc:L1-midstream a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-downstream-operations ;
    skos:definition "The transportation, terminaling, storage, and bulk handling of crude oil, intermediates, and refined products between supply points, refineries, terminals, and downstream distribution locations."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Midstream"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Includes receipt, dispatch, transfer, pipeline, marine, rail, and bulk-truck logistics; terminal and tank-farm operations; inventory management; blending and additive operations where performed outside refinery process units; product segregation; custody transfer; nominations; scheduling; and bulk delivery to downstream depots, customers, or other facilities."@en .

proc:L1-process-excellence-it a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "The enabling function that drives operational excellence through process governance, standardization, performance management, continuous improvement, and transformation; and enables the enterprise through technology strategy, architecture, platforms, infrastructure, cybersecurity, data and integration, and digital capabilities."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Process Excellence & IT"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Includes enterprise process architecture and governance; process ownership, documentation, standardization, measurement, benchmarking, and maturity assessment; continuous improvement, lean/six-sigma methods, automation, and business transformation; enterprise and solution architecture; portfolio, product, project, and demand management; application, data, integration, cloud, infrastructure, network, end-user, and IT service management; cybersecurity, technology risk, resilience, and disaster recovery; and delivery of digital, analytics, AI, and automation capabilities. Enables and governs cross-functional ways of working and enterprise technology. It does not own the business outcomes or physical execution of refining, midstream, distribution, commercial, finance, HR, legal, or EHS processes, except where a specifically delegated enterprise service is modeled as such."@en .

proc:L1-refining a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-downstream-operations ;
    skos:definition "The operation of petroleum refineries to convert crude oil and other hydrocarbon feedstocks into specification-compliant fuels, blendstocks, lubricants, asphalt, petrochemical feedstocks, and other refined products through separation, conversion, treatment, blending, and associated refinery operations."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Refining"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Encompasses refinery production operations and the planning, execution, and recovery activities required to maintain refinery assets, reliability, integrity, safety, and operating availability, including major maintenance and turnarounds."@en .

proc:L1-shared-services a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "An enterprise service-delivery model that consolidates common, repeatable business-support services for multiple business units, legal entities, or regions through a shared organization, standardized processes, common platforms, and defined service levels."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shared Services"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Delivers selected operational and transactional services on behalf of enterprise functions and business domains, including finance operations, HR operations, payroll administration, procurement operations, IT service delivery, master-data administration, customer and supplier support, and other standardized administrative services. Services may be delivered centrally, regionally, or virtually and are governed through service catalogs, service levels, performance measures, and, where applicable, chargeback or cost-allocation arrangements."@en .

proc:L1-supply-chain-mgmt a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Human-authored definition, approved by Hamid (2026-09-18)"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:L0-enabling-functions ;
    skos:definition "The integrated planning, coordination, and optimization of feedstock, intermediate, product, inventory, capacity, logistics, and information flows across the downstream petroleum value chain — from supply and sourcing through refining, terminaling, distribution, and customer fulfilment."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:prefLabel "Supply Chain Mgmt."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Includes demand and supply balancing; sourcing and replenishment planning; production and refinery supply planning; inventory and working-capital optimization; network, terminal, and distribution planning; transportation and delivery planning; materials management; supplier and carrier coordination; performance management; and supply-chain risk and disruption management. It orchestrates, but does not replace, the physical execution performed by refining, midstream, distribution, procurement, and commercial operations."@en .

src:eia-glossary a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
