proc:CM-1-3-10 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3 ;
    skos:definition "Terminal Loading consist of processes such as monitoring customer sales activity and implementing control strategies based upon supply, customer credit and/or contract limitations. Allocation decisions are based on evaluating deals and transaction data to determine which product at the terminal should be made available to the customers. It is responsible for sending locks and unlocks to the terminal when it determines that availability should change."@en ;
